# Change active players and clean removed state

Add Change players to the Board menu and support adding/removing colours on SCR-007.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Change players appears in the Board burger menu and opens SCR-007.
- [x] SCR-007 starts with the persisted active set and supports adding and removing colours.
- [x] At least one player must remain active.
- [x] Removing a player with a hand, plans, roads, settlements, or cities presents: `Removing this player will remove their resources, cards, and plans.` with Cancel and Continue.
- [x] Cancel preserves the player and all state.
- [x] Continue removes the player, their hand, plans, roads, buildings, and ownership entries.
- [x] Removing a player with no associated state takes effect without destructive confirmation.
- [x] Changes persist across termination and dismiss safely to Board.
- [x] Domain and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Added SCR-007 and a Change players Board-menu action with immediate additions/removals.
- Added the exact destructive alert and atomic BoardState cleanup for hands, plans, roads, and buildings.
- Added domain cleanup and UI navigation/addition coverage.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
